  "title": "Saudi Arabia, Turkey, and Pakistan Join Mecca Defence Pact",
  "summary": "Saudi Arabia, Turkey, and Pakistan have signed a joint defense pact in Mecca to counter regional aggression and maintain stability. The pact aims to deter potential threats from Iran and other regional actors, while also establishing mutual military and intelligence cooperation.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "Saudi Arabia, Turkey, and Pakistan signed a joint defense pact on August 7 in Mecca.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The pact includes mutual military assistance and cooperation in intelligence, defense production, logistics, and counter-terrorism.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The pact outlines mutual defense obligations and sets specific terms for the agreement.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
